intervals would be intolerable, and beyond the natural key it fails entirely. Zarlino's remedy (chap. 42, p. 126) is to diminish every Fifth by two-sevenths of a comma, and he proceeds to shew how this affects the tuning. It preserves the small Semitone 24 : 25 = @@R1@@
